
# fs-watch
- label: all fs.watch usage in the server is routed through the facade in src/server/fs-watch.js, which exposes watchTree(dir, onChange), watchFile(path, onChange), and watchCapabilities(); no other src/ module imports watch from node:fs
  command: node --test --test-concurrency=1 test/server/fs-watch.test.js
  tags: [spec, fs-watch, implemented]
- label: watchFile re-arms its underlying watcher when the watched file is replaced by rename, and keeps retrying on a capped exponential backoff (250ms doubling to 30s) while the path does not exist, so a SQLite database that is atomically swapped, deleted and later recreated, or created for the first time after startup all keep producing change events instead of going permanently silent
  command: node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'atomic replacement|deleted and recreated|does not exist yet|backed-off retry' test/server/fs-watch.test.js
  tags: [spec, fs-watch, implemented]
- label: watchTree always uses native recursive watching with no fallback path: package.json pins engines.node >= 22.5.0 (required anyway by node:sqlite), and recursive watching exists on linux from node 20.13 and always on darwin/win32, so no supported runtime lacks it; a runtime that somehow rejects recursion warns once and disables live updates rather than failing silently
  command: node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'recursive support' test/server/fs-watch.test.js && node -e "const e=require('./package.json').engines.node; if(!e||!/>=2[2-9]/.test(e)) process.exit(1)"
  tags: [spec, fs-watch, implemented]

# node-engine
- label: the supported node version is declared in version control and enforced for consistency: package.json engines.node pins the floor (>=22.5.0), .nvmrc pins the matching major for contributors, and every CI/release workflow runs at or above that floor; a test fails if any of the three drift apart or if the floor drops below 20.13, which is the version that makes the fs-watch fallback removal safe
  command: node --test --test-concurrency=1 test/node-engine-contract.test.js
  tags: [spec, node-engine, implemented]
